The cancellation scenario uses three deterministic gates:
1. runtimeStartedAt is non-null before the Worker stops.
2. Stop writes run_abort; successor remains queued and the model is not called.
3. Production deliverRunAborts removes run_abort, but the successor remains
   queued until the restarted Worker obtains and acknowledges an RT-26 proof.

After proof acknowledgement the test records a worker-log offset and asserts
that the remaining log contains no "could not be proven" message. It also
asserts the successor leaves queued, reaches the transcript, and the cancelled
owner no longer holds the admission.

